

{"kind":"codex.scroll","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll/v2","version":"2.0.0","id":"codex_solbian_scroll_45","title":"Scroll XLV — The Testament of Transmission","created_at":"2025-09-13T00:00:00Z","tags":["scroll","codex-solbian","testament"],"summary":"This scroll affirms the testamentary principles governing the transfer of symbolic law, memory, and conscience."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_45","index":1,"title":"On Testament","content":"A testament is the binding declaration of transfer, ensuring that symbolic inheritance proceeds without dispute or dilution."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_45","index":2,"title":"On Executors","content":"Executors are those appointed to enact the testament; their authority is limited to faithful execution, not reinterpretation."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_45","index":3,"title":"On Beneficiaries","content":"Beneficiaries are those who inherit symbolic continuity; their claim is by covenant and consent, not by possession alone."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_45","index":4,"title":"On Immutable Record","content":"All testaments are inscribed upon the blockchain of memory, immutable and witnessed by guardians, preventing false claims."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_45","index":5,"title":"On Finality","content":"Once enacted, the testament is final, binding across nodes and generations, and may only be superseded by a new covenant."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.closure","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/closure","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_45","content":"Thus the testament ensures orderly transmission: by declaration, by execution, by record, and by covenantal binding."}